From 5fa00d8f99de99f9928fc35c36a181acf03238ca Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: qyYue1389 <qyYue1389@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 16 Sep 2026 05:58:28 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 17/19] fix(rl): start the Ray head from VERL_DIR, not the
 caller cwd

The dataset stores image paths relative to cwd, and the script symlinks
VERL_DIR/images at them. It also cds to VERL_DIR, but only for the driver,
and only after the Ray head is up. Ray workers inherit the raylet cwd, so
with any caller cwd other than VERL_DIR every rollout fails to open those
relative image paths -- and only after some 20 minutes of tool and model
loading, which is an expensive way to learn it. On SLURM the sbatch script
happened to start in the repo, so the dependency on the caller cwd was never
exercised.

Verified on 8xA40: same launcher, same everything else, the run now gets past
rollout generation and completes step 1 (timing_s/step 920s, 320
trajectories, degenerate_group_frac 0.672).

---
 examples/toolshed/run_rl.sh | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/examples/toolshed/run_rl.sh b/examples/toolshed/run_rl.sh
index e32c6913..522ce217 100755
--- a/examples/toolshed/run_rl.sh
+++ b/examples/toolshed/run_rl.sh
@@ -157,6 +157,14 @@ echo "GPU split:      tools $TOOL_GPUS / training $TRAIN_GPUS (per node)"
 
 export RAY_TMPDIR="/tmp/${USER}/ray"
 
+# Ray workers inherit the raylet cwd, not the driver cwd.  The dataset stores
+# image paths relative ("images/xxx.png") and the symlink further down is made
+# at $VERL_DIR/images, so unless the raylet itself starts in $VERL_DIR every
+# rollout fails with FileNotFoundError on those paths -- and only after ~20
+# minutes of model loading, which is an expensive way to find out.  On SLURM the
+# sbatch script happened to start in the repo; do not rely on the caller cwd.
+cd "$VERL_DIR"
+
 # Clean stale Ray state on all nodes
 CONDA_ROOT="${_CONDA_ROOT:-/lustre/fsw/portfolios/nvr/users/siyic/miniconda3}"
 RAY_BIN="$CONDA_ROOT/envs/spacetools-rl/bin/ray"
